Operator-authorized single-GPU scaled run on the recovered rig (conductor paused;
ran on stable internal GPU cuda:1, eGPU idle — the eGPU drops under sustained load).
The scaled test removed both confounds of the small-scale BOUNDED result:
  - a LEARNED DECODER (emb->token trained on the EBT's energy-converged embeddings) =
    the fair generation path (vs the earlier simple energy-argmin)
  - 3-digit addition (not memorizable) at 16k steps, where AR reaches 82% (clean headroom)

RESULT (results/thesis_a_part_b_scaled_seed1.json, adversarial-clean): BOUNDED.
  AR@1=0.820, AR@matched=0.840  vs  EBT-argmin=0.000, EBT-descent+decoder=0.000.
AR learns 3-digit addition well (exact "1316","1528","1138","0910"); the EBT generates
INCOHERENT garbage under BOTH decode methods ("5555","====","0=+1","303+") even with a
fully-trained landscape + learned decoder + scale. The learned decoder's CE never
converged (~3 nats ~ uniform), confirming the energy-descended embeddings are not
token-discriminative.

CONCLUSION: energy-as-generator is BOUNDED — the EBT's energy landscape is DISCRIMINATIVE
(part-a held-out margin 0.72) but NOT GENERATIVE; neither a learned decoder nor scale
fixes it. Single seed is decisive (0% vs 82%, confirmed headroom) — no replication needed.
This parallels energy-as-SELECTOR being bounded. Defensible Phase-3 status: both tested
energy mechanisms bounded; verifier product remains the banked deliverable. Invariants
intact (paper_ready, frozen 0.9131, P0.1 honest-negative).

